{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Query is designed to work out of the box with React Native, with the exception of the devtools, which are only supported with React DOM at this time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is a 3rd party "},{"type":"link","href":"https://fbflipper.com/docs/getting-started/react-native/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flipper"}]},{"type":"text","value":" plugin which you can try: https://github.com/bgaleotti/react-query-native-devtools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you would like to help us make the built-in devtools platform agnostic, please let us know!"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"online-status-management","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Online status management"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Query already supports auto refetch on reconnect in web browser.\nTo add this behavior in React Native you have to use React Query "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onlineManager"},{"type":"text","value":" as in the example below:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import NetInfo from '@react-native-community/netinfo'\nimport { onlineManager } from 'react-query'\n\nonlineManager.setEventListener(setOnline => {\n  return NetInfo.addEventListener(state => {\n    setOnline(state.isConnected)\n  })\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"refetch-on-app-focus","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refetch on App focus"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In React Native you have to use React Query "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusManager"},{"type":"text","value":" to refetch when the App is focused."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\nfunction onAppStateChange(status: AppStateStatus) {\n  if (Platform.OS !== 'web') {\n    focusManager.setFocused(status === 'active')\n  }\n}\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const subscription = AppState.addEventListener('change', onAppStateChange)\n\n  return () => subscription.remove()\n}, [])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"refresh-on-screen-focus","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refresh on Screen focus"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In some situations, you may want to refetch the query when a React Native Screen is focused again.\nThis custom hook will call the provided "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetch"},{"type":"text","value":" function when the screen is focused again."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import React from 'react'\nimport { useFocusEffect } from '@react-navigation/native'\n\nexport function useRefreshOnFocus<T>(refetch: () => Promise<T>) {\n  const firstTimeRef = React.useRef(true)\n\n  useFocusEffect(\n    React.useCallback(() => {\n      if (firstTimeRef.current) {\n         firstTimeRef.current = false;\n         return;\n      }\n\n      refetch()\n    }, [refetch])\n  )\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the above code, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetch"},{"type":"text","value":" is skipped the first time because "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useFocusEffect"},{"type":"text","value":" calls our callback on mount in addition to screen focus."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"online-status-management","text":"Online status management","level":2},{"id":"refetch-on-app-focus","text":"Refetch on App focus","level":2},{"id":"refresh-on-screen-focus","text":"Refresh on Screen focus","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nReact Query is designed to work out of the box with React Native, with the exception of the devtools, which are only supported with React DOM at this time.\n\nThere is a 3rd party [Flipper](https://fbflipper.com/docs/getting-started/react-native/) plugin which you can try: https://github.com/bgaleotti/react-query-native-devtools\n\nIf you would like to help us make the built-in devtools platform agnostic, please let us know!\n\n## Online status management\n\nReact Query already supports auto refetch on reconnect in web browser.\nTo add this behavior in React Native you have to use React Query `onlineManager` as in the example below:\n\n```ts\nimport NetInfo from '@react-native-community/netinfo'\nimport { onlineManager } from 'react-query'\n\nonlineManager.setEventListener(setOnline => {\n  return NetInfo.addEventListener(state => {\n    setOnline(state.isConnected)\n  })\n})\n```\n\n## Refetch on App focus\n\nIn React Native you have to use React Query `focusManager` to refetch when the App is focused.\n\n```ts\nimport { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\nfunction onAppStateChange(status: AppStateStatus) {\n  if (Platform.OS !== 'web') {\n    focusManager.setFocused(status === 'active')\n  }\n}\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const subscription = AppState.addEventListener('change', onAppStateChange)\n\n  return () => subscription.remove()\n}, [])\n```\n\n## Refresh on Screen focus\n\nIn some situations, you may want to refetch the query when a React Native Screen is focused again.\nThis custom hook will call the provided `refetch` function when the screen is focused again.\n\n```ts\nimport React from 'react'\nimport { useFocusEffect } from '@react-navigation/native'\n\nexport function useRefreshOnFocus<T>(refetch: () => Promise<T>) {\n  const firstTimeRef = React.useRef(true)\n\n  useFocusEffect(\n    React.useCallback(() => {\n      if (firstTimeRef.current) {\n         firstTimeRef.current = false;\n         return;\n      }\n\n      refetch()\n    }, [refetch])\n  )\n}\n```\n\nIn the above code, `refetch` is skipped the first time because `useFocusEffect` calls our callback on mount in addition to screen focus.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: react-native\ntitle: React Native\n---\n\nReact Query is designed to work out of the box with React Native, with the exception of the devtools, which are only supported with React DOM at this time.\n\nThere is a 3rd party [Flipper](https://fbflipper.com/docs/getting-started/react-native/) plugin which you can try: https://github.com/bgaleotti/react-query-native-devtools\n\nIf you would like to help us make the built-in devtools platform agnostic, please let us know!\n\n## Online status management\n\nReact Query already supports auto refetch on reconnect in web browser.\nTo add this behavior in React Native you have to use React Query `onlineManager` as in the example below:\n\n```ts\nimport NetInfo from '@react-native-community/netinfo'\nimport { onlineManager } from 'react-query'\n\nonlineManager.setEventListener(setOnline => {\n  return NetInfo.addEventListener(state => {\n    setOnline(state.isConnected)\n  })\n})\n```\n\n## Refetch on App focus\n\nIn React Native you have to use React Query `focusManager` to refetch when the App is focused.\n\n```ts\nimport { focusManager } from 'react-query'\n\nfunction onAppStateChange(status: AppStateStatus) {\n  if (Platform.OS !== 'web') {\n    focusManager.setFocused(status === 'active')\n  }\n}\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const subscription = AppState.addEventListener('change', onAppStateChange)\n\n  return () => subscription.remove()\n}, [])\n```\n\n## Refresh on Screen focus\n\nIn some situations, you may want to refetch the query when a React Native Screen is focused again.\nThis custom hook will call the provided `refetch` function when the screen is focused again.\n\n```ts\nimport React from 'react'\nimport { useFocusEffect } from '@react-navigation/native'\n\nexport function useRefreshOnFocus<T>(refetch: () => Promise<T>) {\n  const firstTimeRef = React.useRef(true)\n\n  useFocusEffect(\n    React.useCallback(() => {\n      if (firstTimeRef.current) {\n         firstTimeRef.current = false;\n         return;\n      }\n\n      refetch()\n    }, [refetch])\n  )\n}\n```\n\nIn the above code, `refetch` is skipped the first time because `useFocusEffect` calls our callback on mount in addition to screen focus.\n"}
